{{Quote|This is where the Senate gathers to discuss many pressing issues and legislation. Where the future of the galaxy is decided. For better or worse.|[[Riyo Chuchi]], to [[Omega]]|<ref name="Truth and Consequences">{{TBB|Truth and Consequences}}</ref>}}
The '''Imperial Senate Building''', formerly known as the '''Galactic Senate Building''', also known as the '''Senate Building''', '''Senate Rotunda''', or the '''Senate Dome''' was an immense building located on the [[planet]] [[Coruscant]] that served as the seat of the [[Galactic Republic]] [[Galactic Senate|Senate]] and later the [[Imperial Senate]] of the [[Galactic Empire]].

Located in the heart of Coruscant, the Galactic Senate Building was surrounded by the [[Federal District|Senate District]], including the [[Imperial Executive Building|Senate Office Building]] where the Supreme Chancellor had his [[Emperor's office|offices]].<ref name="GalacticSenate" /> With its iconic domed shape, the mighty structure was easy to spot. The building and the Senate district were protected by the [[Color|blue]] [[robe]]d [[Senate Guard]]s who stood watch and blended in with the formal surroundings of the Senate Building. They could also be found at the entrances to many of the delegate platforms and at the entrances to the building itself. Colossal statues outside the building commemorated the Republic's ancient founders.

At the center of the building was the large, rotund [[Galactic Senate Chamber]]. It held seats on circular platforms for the hundreds of [[senator]]s and delegates who would meet to pass laws and discuss legislation. When a member wished to speak, the platform could disconnect from the wall, allowing the member to be seen and heard by all others. In the center was a podium from which the [[Supreme Chancellor]] would direct the business of the Senate. The Senate Building also contained many smaller meeting rooms, senatorial offices, including the [[Chancellor's working office|working office]] of the chancellor, and other administrative facilities. To allow easy access for diplomats, a docking bay was built along one side of the building.

==Description==
===Location and complex===
[[File:Imperial_plaza_Andor_S2E7.png|left|thumb|290x290px|The Imperial Plaza complex connecting the Senate Building with the Imperial Executive building]]
The building housing the [[Galactic Senate|Galactic]] and later the [[Imperial Senate]] sessions<ref name="DatabankSenate">{{Databank|galactic-senate|Galactic Senate}}</ref> was known as the Galactic Senate Building during the reign of the [[Galactic Republic]]<ref name="AbEverything">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know]]''</ref> and renamed the Imperial Senate Building<ref name="Thrawn">[[Thrawn (novel)|''Thrawn'']]</ref> under the [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="ROTS" /> It also became known by many names including the Senate Rotunda<ref name="Senate Guard SWE">{{SWE|groups|senateguard|Senate Guard}}</ref> Senate Dome,<ref name="Catalyst">''[[Catalyst: A Rogue One Novel]]''</ref> or simply the Senate Building.<ref name="UltimateSW">''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''</ref> It was an enormous oval-shaped structure<ref name="Complete New">''[[Star Wars: Complete Locations, New Edition]]''</ref> 2 [[kilometer]]s in diameter,<ref name="CL2016" /> located in the [[Imperial Plaza]]<ref name="Tark" /> at the heart of the [[capital]] [[planet]] [[Coruscant]]'s [[Federal District]].<ref name="Complete New" /> The building easily stood out from the surrounding skyline<ref name="VE">''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''</ref> thanks to its distinctive shape.<ref name="Complete New" />

Leading to the building's official entrance was the [[Avenue of the Core Founders]], a vast concourse<ref name="Complete New" /> adorned with the statues of the Galactic Republic's [[Core Worlds]] founders,<ref name="AbEverything" /> a feature that became controversial over time as more non-[[humanoid]] cultures joined the Republic.<ref name="Complete New" /> During the [[Imperial Era]], a large pool was added to the Plaza, running parallel to<ref name="Ghorman">{{Andor|Ever Been to Ghorman?}}</ref> the [[Senate arcade building]]<ref name="AD">{{Andor|Welcome to the Rebellion}} {{C|audio description from [[Disney+]]}}</ref> whose ground floor housed the [[Senate Garage]] and [[Senate Cafe|cafe]].<ref name="WTTR-Script">{{Disney|subdomain=assets.debut|url=documents/Andor%20209%20--%20POST%20FINAL%20--%203.3.24%5B1%5D.pdf|text=Episode #209 "Welcome To The Rebellion" Script|format=PDF}} {{C|page 15}}</ref> The Plaza and auxiliary structure directly connected the Senate Building to the [[Imperial Executive Building]],<ref name="Welcome">{{Andor|Welcome to the Rebellion}}</ref> which housed Senate offices and working spaces,<ref name="UltimateSW" /> allowing Senators to commute between the two buildings on foot<ref name="Welcome" /> and have meetings in the large open space<ref name="Ghorman" /> as well as inside the large [[Atrium (Imperial Plaza)|Atrium]].<ref name="Welcome AD">{{Andor|Welcome to the Rebellion}} {{AD|Disney+}}</ref> The [[Galactic Senate Medcenter]] was also located in the complex, to provide top-notch [[medical]] care for all senators and encourage participation to the legislature.<ref name="Coruscant">{{EncyclopediaCite|Coruscant}}</ref>

===Interior features===
====Galactic Senate Chamber====
{{Main|Galactic Senate Chamber}}
[[File:Galacticsenate.png|thumb|290x290px|The Galactic Senate chamber]]
The building's main feature, which took up the biggest part of its interior space,<ref name="Complete New" /> was the [[Galactic Senate Chamber]], the vast room where Senate sessions took place.<ref name="TPM" /> The room's walls were lined with 1,024 [[repulsorpod]]s<ref name="UltimateSW" /> which housed more than 1,000 Senators,<ref name="Complete New" /> [[Senior Senator]]s<ref name="Welcome" /> and [[Junior Representative]]s representing the various member planets of the Republic and the Empire.<ref name="UltimateSW" /> As it received no natural sunlight or air, the chamber's ceiling was lined with lights which, along with its [[atmosphere|artificial atmosphere]], were carefully designed to diminish senators' sense of time to allow debates to continue without being affected by nightfall. It was also equipped with [[holorecorder]]s,<ref name="Complete New" /> voice-amplifying [[microphone]]s and translators,<ref name="UltimateSW" /> which fed directly to the media complex and data center located above the Chamber as well as to the screens in the Senators' pods.<ref name="Complete New" />

At the center of the room was the 30-[[meter]] tall [[Chancellor's Podium]], which retracted from the [[Chancellor's working office]] underneath the rotunda and hosted the [[Supreme Chancellor]] and the [[Chair of the Senate]]. A select team including the [[Parliamentarian]], [[Official Reporter]] and the [[Journal Clerk]] sat on the podium's lower level and helped regulate the proceedings, while the [[Sergeant-at-Arms]] supervised the multiple [[Senate hovercam droid]]s<ref name="Complete New" /> that flew around the chamber and recorded closer looks of the Senators' speeches.<ref name="TPM" /> 

====Senate offices====
[[File:Senate_Hall.png|left|thumb|270x270px|A section of the public corridor]]
Surrounding the Senate Chamber were 1 kilometer of offices - including Senator-exclusive chambers and public lobbying rooms;the two were separated by the public corridor, which ran the entire length of the Senate Building and was always busy with aides, pages and workers. The various levels of the corridor could be reached via private or commuter [[turbolift]]s, with the latter being able to service up to 50 general staff at a time. There were also both horizontal and vertical turbolifts which connected the delegations' inner offices with each other, allowing Senators to come in contact with each other for secret meetings and dealmaking.<ref name="Complete New" />

Most offices were uniquely designed, incporporating elements from the Senator's native culture, including building materials and architectural style. The senator-exclusive offices were located directly behind the Senate pods and were reserved for the senators and their high-level aides, incorporating conference rooms and relaxation areas. They were highly secured, with the floors separated with an alarmed anti-[[saboteur]] mesh, and restricted to outsiders, including even [[Senate Guard]]s. Beyond the public corridor were the outer offices, where Senate committees, workers and aides did much of the laborious paperwork to assist each delegation with its public duties.<ref name="Complete New" />

====Administrative and press facilities====
[[File:Andor-EscapeFromTheSenate.png|thumb|270x270px|ISB agent Beska tries to arrest Mon Mothma in the press deck for Gate 9 of the Senate Building]]
To serve arrivals and departures,<ref name="VE" /> a number of [[shuttle]] [[hangar]]s were built<ref name="Complete New" /> on the side of the building,<ref name="VE" /> right at the base of the dome.<ref name="Complete New" /> There was also a [[dining commons]]<ref name="Senate Spy" /> serving dishes from around [[the galaxy]],<ref name="Complete New" /> and was a popular meeting place for Senators.<ref name="Senate Spy" /> The building was also equipped with loading docks<ref name="Welcome" /> and a sewage recylcing facility at [[sublevel nine]].<ref name="Queen's Shadow">''[[Queen's Shadow]]''</ref>

The dome of the building was crested with five [[Long-Range Antenna]] clusters to transmit senate rulings, all controlled from the media complex on top of the Senate Chamber.<ref name="Complete New" /> Press and journalists were accommodated in several news bays managed by a kiosk on the building's ground floor; accredited journalists not assigned to a bay were allowed to "float" around, recording speeches from shared rooms at senate Gates with mounted [[viewscreen]]s.<ref name="Welcome" />

===Security===
[[File:Senate_entrance_Andor_S2E7.png|left|thumb|290x290px|Senate Security guards stand watch on an entrance to the building]]
During the Republic era, the building was guarded by the [[Senate Guard]], a highly trained<ref name="Senate Guard">{{Databank|senate-guard|Senate Guard}}</ref> unit which also guarded the Senate District alongside the [[Coruscant Security Force]].<ref name="UltimateSW" /> The Guard also accompanied the [[Supreme Chancellor]] as his personal protective force.<ref name="AotC">{{Film|II}}</ref> The very best troopers of the guard were handpicked to serve as [[Senate Commando]]s, a more active unit which also undertook special missions on behalf of the Republic.<ref name="Senate Guard" />

During the Imperial era, the task of ceremonial Senate guard was passed onto the successors of the Republic unit, renamed the [[Imperial Senate Guard]]. The unit consisted of soldiers loyal to the [[New Order]] and the Galactic Emperor, who were also tasked with protecting Senators and the District.<ref name="Imperial Senate Guard">{{FFGTCG|set=A Wretched Hive|cardname=Imperial Senate Guard|link=opposition-cycle/a-wretched-hive/imperial-senate-guard-r1805}}</ref> Access to the building was controlled via checkpoints consisting of [[DeTECHt]] [[security scanner]]s and manned by [[Senate Security]] agents in every one of the several ground-floor entrances. Anyone entering the building had to display their pass and stand in the [[scanner]] before being allowed to enter into the main hall;<ref name="Messenger">{{Andor|Messenger}}</ref> from there, Senators could access the public corridors through Gates including [[Gate 9]], which consisted of a guarded waiting area for journalists and a private turbolift for Senators and their aides.<ref name="Welcome" /> The building was also secretly equipped with an [[Imperial Security Bureau]] complex on the basement.<ref name="Complete New" />

==History==
===Establishment of the Senate and early years===
[[File:Senate_Plaza_by_night.png|thumb|right|250px|The Senate Building by night.]]
The [[Galactic Senate]] was founded in around [[1032 BBY]],<ref name="Date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the [[Defeat of the Sith|supposed destruction of the Sith]] to [[1032 BBY]]. As the novel [[Tarkin (novel)|''Tarkin'']] states the [[Galactic Senate]] was founded in the immediate aftermath of the supposed destruction, it must have been founded in around 1032 [['ABY-BBY' dating system|BBY]].</ref> following the [[defeat of the Sith]] in the [[Jedi-Sith War]].<ref name="Tarkin">[[Tarkin (novel)|''Tarkin'']]</ref> It was meant to be the legislative body of the nascent [[Galactic Republic]], where representatives of all member [[planet]]s would get an equal chance to speak.<ref name="TPM" /> During its early years, the Senate was housed in a small [[debating chamber]] on the planet [[Coruscant]], until it was eventually moved to the far larger Galactic Senate Building.<ref name="Complete New" />

During the [[High Republic Era]], the Senate Building was also the location of choice for the [[Trial of Marchion Ro|trial]] of [[Marchion Ro]], the so-called [[Eye of the Nihil]] who had led the [[Nihil]] marauders through their [[Nihil conflict|conflict]] with the Republic. Unrepentant, Ro chose to mock the gathered Senate as an ineffective government that chose to do nothing despite its near-limitless power, whereas he, a single man, had done "everything." For his crimes, including his plan to use the [[blight]] to wipe out all life in [[the galaxy]], Ro was sentenced to a life of solitary confinement in deep space without the possibility of parole.<ref name="Trials of the Jedi">''[[The High Republic: Trials of the Jedi]]''</ref>

===Fall of the Republic===
[[File:Displate-YodaandPalpatine.png|thumb|left|300px|The Senate Building stands as the site of a duel between the Dark Lord of the Sith Darth Sidious and Jedi Grand Master Yoda.]]
By [[32 BBY]], the Senate's status had diminished considerably, with corruption and bribery running rampant. Political turmoil engulfed the Republic,<ref name="TPM" /> which ultimately led to the creation of the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]], a union of planets and corporations who wished to secede from the Republic altogether.<ref name="AotC" /> The eruption of the [[Clone Wars]] in [[22 BBY]]<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> resulted in the first open warfare in centuries.<ref name="AotC" /> The Galactic Senate became the target of several attacks, including the [[bombing of Coruscant's central power distribution grid]] which damaged the building, severing its power supply and interrupting a vital voting session.<ref name="PoP">{{TCW|Pursuit of Peace}}</ref> [[Bounty hunter]] [[Cad Bane]] also infiltrated the Executive Building, taking several senators hostage until he was driven away by the [[Coruscant Security Force]] and [[Jedi Knight]] [[Anakin Skywalker]], in what became known as the [[Senate hostage crisis]].<ref name="HC">{{TCW|Hostage Crisis}}</ref>

In [[19 BBY]], [[Supreme Chancellor]] Palpatine was discovered by the Jedi to be [[Dark Lord of the Sith]] Darth Sidious; in response, he executed [[Order 66]] which called for the elimination of all Jedi by their [[clone trooper]]s and transformed the republic into the [[Galactic Empire]]. [[Grand Master]] [[Yoda]] confronted Palpatine in his working office in the Chancellery Secretariat, and the two were engaged in a [[lightsaber duel]] in the Senate Chamber. The duel severely damaged the rotunda, with the two [[Force-sensitive]]s hurling Senate pods at one another; Yoda was ultimately forced to escape through a duct, leaving Palpatine victorious.<ref name="ROTS" />

===Imperial Senate===
Following the establishment of the Empire, the building was renamed the Imperial Senate Building to reflect the new government.<ref name="Complete New" /> Although the rotunda retained its appearance during the first several years,<ref name="Truth and Consequences" /> by [[5 BBY]] a grand [[Imperial crest]] was painted in the bottom of the chamber, under the speaker's podium; the same symbol was etched in the Senators' pods.<ref name="The Eye">{{Andor|The Eye}}</ref> The outside of the building remained unchanged, as the new government attempted to retain aesthetic ties to its predecessor.<ref name="Complete New" /> By [[2 BBY]] the Empire also renovated the Imperial Plaza, adding a reflective pool and an arcade building connecting the Senate to the Executive Building.<ref name="Welcome" />

